 innocent civilians including  children women journalists and medical  and humanitarian personnel is a grave  breach of international humanitarian law  and constitutes war crimes  perpetrators of such acts must be  identified and held accountable japan  has referred the situation in ukraine to  the international criminal code and we  look forward to continued progress in  the investigation by prosecutor current  we would like to continue to contribute  to the icc's activities while  maintaining close conduct with the icc  and its state parties  sustaining peace will never be achieved  without tackling impunity japan will  continue to work together with our  partner to this end thank you  i thank the representative of japan and  give the floor to the representative of  chile  okay the representative of chile is not  here they will be submitting their  statement in writing and with that i'd  like to thank all our briefers and  member states for their participation  and contribution we feel very encouraged  by the level of interest and  engagement on a matter of crucial  importance such as assuring  accountability for atrocities committed  in ukraine the legal threshold for  providing war crimes and crimes against  humanity is high as  most of you here said and the system has  in the past proved torturous in its  proceedings and slow to deliver justice  but ukraine and russia are still at war  and to really respond to the scale of  russia's attack we have to connect what  is happening today to the violations  from the past to show how they have a  way of repeating over and over again we  have to tell not just the stories of  people hurt and and killed in this war  but also the history culture and the way  of life putin is trying to wipe out  our aim is one only to ensure justice  both in normal courts and in the court  of public opinion which is a key  ingredient to keep us alert and to  mobilize political action to support  justice everywhere in thanking you once  again for your active participation this  meeting is adjourned
 

